Chapter: WaveletSortAliasing

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Signal chapter Wavelet

 Locks in the dwt-insert aliasing fix. list-set-at mutates in place
 and arguments evaluate left to right, so the swap's second read of
 slot i must happen before the first write lands. Before the fix the
 inner set stored slot i minus one into slot i, then the outer
 argument re-read slot i and wrote that same value back down: the
 sort filled with duplicates instead of swapping, and dwt-compress
 picked its threshold from a corrupted ranking.

Section: Definitions

  print-list : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  print-list (xs) (i) (len) = act
    if i >= len then print-line-uni "done"
    else act
      print-line-uni (show (list-at xs i))
      print-list xs (i + 1) len
    end
  end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-list (dwt-insertion-sort [5, 3, 4, 1, 2] 0 5) 0 5
  end

